## Section 2: Weekly Schedule & Prep Rhythm

### Weekday Sessions (2-3 sessions/week, ~30-45 min each)
- 2 problems per session, following NeetCode 150 pattern order strictly
- Attempt first (~20 min), review solution/discussion only if stuck
- Add retrospective header comment before moving on

### Weekend Session (1 session, 2-4 hours — Saturday OR Sunday, not both)
| Time | Activity |
|---|---|
| First 1-1.5 hrs | Review week's problems — revisit anything struggled with |
| Next 1-1.5 hrs | System design: read Grokking chapter → sketch design → write doc |
| Last 30 min | Behavioral: write or refine one STAR story |

### Monthly Checkpoint (last Sunday of each month)
- Review `docs/progress.md`
- Identify weakest pattern → allocate extra focus next month
- Do one timed mock problem (no hints, 45 min hard cutoff)

### 3-4 Month Arc

| Month | Algorithm Focus | System Design |
|---|---|---|
| 1 | Arrays, Two Pointers, Sliding Window, Stack, Binary Search | URL Shortener, Rate Limiter, Pastebin |
| 2 | Linked List, Trees, Tries, Heap/Priority Queue | News Feed, Notification System, Chat System |
| 3 | Backtracking, Graphs, DP (1D + 2D) | Search Autocomplete, YouTube/Netflix, Web Crawler |
| 4 | Greedy, mock interviews, review | Distributed KV Store, Twitter, Message Queue |

